In the previous answer, the issue was due to the return statement in the `put` method. When the document is already archived (i.e., its body is `None`), the method returns `(409, body)`, where `body` is `None`. This caused the issue when unpacking the return value into two variables.

In the corrected code, I changed the return statement in the `put` method to `(409, self.documents[doc_id])`. This way, when the document is already archived, the method returns `(409, None)`, which is correctly unpacked into two variables.
